      "summary": "Requests vulnerable to .netrc credentials leak via malicious URLs\n### Impact\n\nDue to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\n### Workarounds\nFor older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\n### References\nhttps",
      "title": "GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7 \u2014 OSV advisory",
      "url": "https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7"
